# Copy this file to cluster.conf (same directory) and fill in for your
# allocation. cluster.conf itself is gitignored — never committed, since
# partition/account strings are specific to whoever's running this and to
# which cluster.
#
# Read by shells/slurm/submit.sh, which passes SLURM_PARTITION/SLURM_ACCOUNT/
# SLURM_GRES to `sbatch` on the command line (SLURM directives are parsed
# from the job script itself before any shell code runs, so they can't be
# sourced from a file at submit time — this is the workaround). The job
# scripts under shells/slurm/*.slurm.sh also source this file directly for
# SCRATCH_DIR, which is real runtime shell code.

# Required.
SLURM_PARTITION=
SLURM_ACCOUNT=

# Optional — defaults shown.
SLURM_GRES=gpu:1

# Where large caches (HF_HOME) should live instead of $HOME. See notes/hpc.md
# for why — $HOME is often small-quota/network-mounted on HPC, and HF_HOME
# alone (pi05/Robometer weights + lerobot/libero dataset) was 155GB on the
# dev machine this was built on.
SCRATCH_DIR=/scratch/$USER
